meta {
  name: CORS preflight (blocked origin)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

options {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/send?brand=acme
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Origin: https://evil.example
  Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 403
}

docs {
  # CORS preflight — blocked origin

  `https://evil.example` is not in the `acme` brand's `allowedOrigins`, so the
  preflight is rejected with `403` and **no** CORS headers. The browser then
  refuses to send the actual `POST`, so a form on a non-allowlisted origin can
  never submit to this brand.
}
